      "title": "The limiting sum of a geometric series",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "chs2020e1-q9",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "stem": "A geometric series \\(1-\\frac1x+\\frac{1}{x^2}-\\frac{1}{x^3}+\\dots\\) has limiting sum \\(S\\).\nFor what values of \\(x\\) is \\(S\\lt 1\\)?",
          "hint": "First require |r| < 1, then compare S = x/(x + 1) with 1.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Identify the first term and common ratio. A limiting sum exists only when \\(|r|<1\\).",
              "work": "\\(a=1,\\quad r=-\\frac1x,\\quad |r|<1\\Rightarrow\\left|\\frac1x\\right|<1\\Rightarrow |x|>1\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Use the convergent geometric-series formula.",
              "work": "\\(S=\\frac{a}{1-r}=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac1x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\\quad (|x|>1)\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Compare \\(S\\) with 1 by subtracting 1.",
              "work": "\\(S-1=\\frac{x}{x+1}-1=-\\frac1{x+1}\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "On the allowed domain \\(|x|>1\\), if \\(x>1\\), then \\(x+1>0\\), so \\(S-1<0\\). If \\(x<-1\\), then \\(x+1<0\\), so \\(S-1>0\\).",
              "work": "\\(x>1\\Rightarrow S<1;\\qquad x<-1\\Rightarrow S>1\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Therefore only the positive part of the convergence domain satisfies the inequality.",
              "work": "\\(\\boxed{x>1}\\quad\\text{(option D)}\\)"
            }
          ],
          "xp": 1,
          "meta": {
            "source": "Caringbah 2020 3U Trials & Solutions",
            "school": "Caringbah High School",
            "year": 2020,
            "number": "9"
          },
          "options": [
            "\\(x\\gt -1\\)",
            "\\(x\\gt -1,\\ x\\neq0\\)",
            "\\(x\\gt 0\\)",
            "\\(x\\gt 1\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 3,
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "has limiting sum",
              "note": "A limiting sum needs |r| = |1/x| < 1, so |x| > 1."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
